    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Bryce Harper** (80.21) serving as our undisputed anchor. Facing Scherzer, **Harper** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill adjustment and a favorable BvP history, making him the highest-upside play despite the looming 30% rain risk. **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Justin Crawford** (69.88) also present elite scoring profiles in the same matchup, with **Crawford** particularly intriguing given the high-efficiency environment created by Scherzer\u2019s vulnerability. **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) rounds out our strongest group; he is in a prime position to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Jobe, buoyed by a wind-out benefit and a solidified #2 spot in the order.\n\nThe marginal start decision was tight, ultimately favoring **Jonathan Aranda** (56.76) over **Gavin Sheets** (50.45) for the utility spot. While **Sheets** provided a decent floor against Lambert, the optimizer prioritized **Aranda** due to his superior platoon advantage (12% boost) against Kirby, assuming he maintains that #2 lineup placement. **Lawrence Butler** (53.97) remains in the lineup despite a 13% negative platoon adjustment, justified by the wind-out boost providing enough cushion to keep his daily efficiency in our starting range. Conversely, **Brendan Donovan** (47.47) was the toughest exclusion from the bench; his platoon edge was neutralized by the presence of a tough arm in Griffin Jax, leading us to favor the slightly higher ceilings of our active starters. We remain vigilant on the weather situation for **Harper**, **Arraez**, and **Crawford**, as any significant delay or cancellation could force us to re-evaluate our approach to the daily game caps for the remainder of the week.",
